From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Widen license-files to cover the vendored libpg_query/postgres licences

pyproject.toml sets a PEP 639 license-files = ["LICENSE"] list, so
setuptools never falls back to its LICEN[CS]E* default glob (CLAUDE.md
gotcha 105): the extension statically links libpg_query (BSD-3-Clause,
libpg_query/LICENSE) and the PostgreSQL parser it vendors
(libpg_query/src/postgres/COPYRIGHT), and neither licence ships in the
wheel's dist-info/licenses/ even though both are compiled directly into
pgparse's .so. Verified against the real published pgparse-1.0.3 wheels
on PyPI, which have the same gap.

The build workflow copies libpg_query/LICENSE and
libpg_query/src/postgres/COPYRIGHT to LICENSE.libpg_query and
LICENSE.postgres at the project root before the build runs; this patch
is what makes setuptools actually package them.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 3f4a0b9..8569cfb 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ version = "1.0.3"
 description = "Python wrapper for libpg_query"
 readme = "README.md"
 license = "BSD-3-Clause"
-license-files = ["LICENSE"]
+license-files = ["LICENSE", "LICENSE.libpg_query", "LICENSE.postgres"]
 authors = [
     {name = "Gavin M. Roy", email = "gavinmroy@gmail.com"}
 ]
--
